<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>Write an Equation to Model Data</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01209</md:content-id>
    <md:title>Write an Equation to Model Data</md:title>
    <md:uuid>d0c34c5d-ceb2-4fc1-aca4-43dae7f02aa8</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para>For questions 1 - 2 , use the following prompt and image.</para>
      <para>
        <quote>The image shows the battery usage of a cell phone 9 hours after it was fully charged. It also shows a prediction that the battery would last 8 more hours.</quote>
      </para>
      <para>
        <figure>
          <media alt="graph of battery usage">
            <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_22_04_01.png"/>
          </media>
        </figure>
      </para>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
        <item> Write an equation for a model that fits the data in the image and gives the percent of battery power as a function of time since the phone was fully charged. Be prepared to show your reasoning.
</item>
      </list>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
        <item> Based on your function, what percentage of power would the battery have 4 hours after this image was taken? What about 5 hours after the image was taken? Be prepared to show your reasoning. </item>
      </list>
      <para>For questions 3 - 5, use the following prompt and images.</para>
      <para>
        <quote>Here are two more images showing the battery usage at two later times, before the battery was charged again.</quote>
      </para>
      <para>
        <figure>
          <media alt="Two images of advanced battery usage, 29 percent and 7 percent.">
            <image mime-type="image/png" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_22_04_02.png"/>
          </media>
        </figure>
      </para>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
        <item> How well did the function you wrote predict the battery power 4 and 5 hours after the first image was taken (that is, 13 and 14 hours after the battery was fully charged)? Be prepared to show your reasoning. </item>
      </list>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
        <item> What do you notice about the change in the prediction between \( t=13 \) and \( t=14 \)?</item>
      </list>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" type="enumerated">
        <item> Write a new equation for a function that would better fit the data shown in the last image. </item>
      </list>
      <div class="os-raise-usermessage-lightbulb">
        <para>If you get stuck, consider creating a table of values or a scatter plot of the data. </para>
      </div>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
